      "path": "cordis.patch.yml",
      "text": "# onekey-models bundle patch.\n#\n# The row id MUST equal the package name. DSH addresses a bundle's settings\n# namespace by its **mount row id** (SettingsForms.describe() publishes\n# `entry.options.id`), while the bundle's own card in the plugin page is keyed by\n# the **package name** (`plugins.bundle.config` renders with `{ entryKey:\n# pkg.name }`). When the two disagree the card reads no namespace at all and\n# every control stays dead with no error printed anywhere — this is exactly the\n# trap documented in dsh-jev-tools/cordis.patch.yml.\n#\n# One insert row mounts the Host half. The browser half is declared in\n# package.json under `dsh.client` and binds to this row.\n- insert:\n    - id: onekey-models\n      name: onekey-models\n      config: {}"
    }
